    "result_text": "The full suite passes (`BUILD SUCCESS`). `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class in the project.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-email-domain blocklist in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` (the controller handling `POST /api/owners`):\n\n1. **Added the blocklist constant** \u2014 `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` = `{mailinator.com, tempmail.com, guerrillamail.com}`, alongside the existing `EMAIL_PATTERN`.\n2. **Added a `java.util.Set` import.**\n3. **Wired the check into `normalizeAndValidateFields`** \u2014 right after the email is normalized (trimmed/lower-cased) and syntactically validated. If the domain is blocklisted, the method returns `false`, which the `addOwner` handler already translates into `400 BAD_REQUEST`.\n4. **Added the `isDisposableEmailDomain` helper** that extracts the domain after the last `@` and tests membership case-insensitively (the email is already lower-cased by the caller).\n\nI placed the check on the create flow's email validation path, matching where the specification's rule applies (the acceptance test posts `x@mailinator.com` and expects 400). Reusing the existing normalize-and-validate seam kept it consistent with how the other email/address/telephone rules reject with 400.\n\nThe targeted acceptance test (`errorRejectsDisposableDomain`) and the full test suite both pass.",
